        "text": "The Secret Garden's Threshold",
        "variant": "h2"
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "paragraph_1": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "Elara traced the crumbling mortar of the old garden wall, its stones swallowed by ivy and forgotten for decades. Locals whispered tales of a forgotten estate, but she’d only ever found overgrown brambles and silence beyond its weathered façade. Today, a glint of moss-covered brass caught her eye – a handle, almost entirely obscured. With a grunt, she pushed, and the ancient wood groaned open, revealing not more decay, but a blinding emerald light.",
        "variant": "body"
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "paragraph_2": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "The air shifted, thick with the scent of jasmine and something else, something impossibly sweet and alive. Before her lay a world untamed, yet exquisitely ordered. Trees with leaves of iridescent silver shimmered under a perpetually soft, golden light. Flowers she’d never seen before bloomed in impossible hues, their petals unfurling in slow, deliberate dances. A crystal-clear stream wound through the landscape, its waters humming with a faint, melodic tune. This wasn't just a garden; it was a breath held, a secret kept, waiting for someone to finally step inside. Elara, mesmerized, took that step.",
        "variant": "body"
      },
      "children": []
    }
  }
